// The gatekeeper this fix could most easily have broken, checked in the
// one pipeline where movecheck is not there to catch it first.
//
// Before the fix, *every* reachable `void` conditional failed codegen --
// including the ill-formed ones -- because the merge block always built
// a named phi. Making the legal ones compile removes that accidental
// gate, so the value positions have to be rejected by something real.
// They are: the conditional now hands back its arms' own `void`-typed
// value, which makes it indistinguishable from a plain `void` call to
// every consumer, and check_store_type rejects it here with exactly the
// message `int x = h();` gets -- "type mismatch initializing/assigning
// variable 'x'".
//
// tests/movetest_source/void_conditional_bound_to_a_variable_is_rejected
// is the same program seen by the frontend, which is what actually
// diagnoses it for a user: the full driver runs check_moves first, so
// this codegen-only path is the backstop, not the diagnostic.
//
// (Honest note: this case also fails on the pre-fix compiler, but for
// the *wrong* reason -- the invalid-IR verifier failure. `throws:`
// compares only the error kind, and both are CodegenError. Its value is
// forward-looking, as a guard on the backstop.)
int taken = 0;
void h() { taken = 1; }
void h2() { taken = 2; }

int main() {
    bool c = true;
    int x = c ? h() : h2();
    return x;
}
